# B7, Andrew's #8, by hand: a player pours sand on one spot, walks up the pile
# and down the far side, digs in it, and does it all again from a replay.
# Everything here is player input: place, break, the walking keys.
#   triangulum --play scripts/b7-walk.play --out out/b7/walk
#
# T2: the beach here is no longer flat (the land falls towards the water, a
# block every three or four columns inland), and a pile poured on a slope
# runs downhill. So the pour and the walk up it stand on a sand sheet laid
# over the beach: sand at layers 1023..1025 (the sand block the assert
# below names is the sheet's as much as the beach's) from the player's
# column eight columns inland and eight across, the air above cleared, and
# a sandstone kerb at layer 1024 along the two sides where the beach drops
# away, so nothing slides off the sheet. The box cuts no natural sand, so
# nothing ravels. alt_agl is measured against the natural ground, which the
# sheet stands a block over at the pour, as the old beach's surface stood
# over its own height; past the sheet the walk goes on up the natural
# beach. The poured blocks fall onto what came before and spread as they
# land (the levels rule), which is what makes a pile of them. Editing this
# chunk wakes the sea along its sides when the region is built (the shore
# is not at rest as generated): about 4,200 units move and settle inside
# 200 ticks, and the films they leave dry in patches over the next
# thousand, so the sheet gets 1,200 ticks (an even number: the pour keeps
# its tick parity) before the recording starts.
sim powder levels 35
sun 35
mode fly
atblock 1 1911 59004 1025
sim off
fill 0 -3 -3 7 4 -1 sand
fill -1 -4 -2 7 -4 -2 sandstone
fill -1 -3 -2 -1 4 -2 sandstone
fill 0 -3 0 7 4 10 air
sim on
tick 1200
assert queued == 0
assert block[1,1911,59004,1023] == sand
mode walk
hotbar sand,gravel,stone,dirt
select 1
lookaxis +i 0
wait 0.5
assert on_ground == true
replay record b7-walk.replay

# ---- pour on one spot ----------------------------------------------------------
# Five blocks ahead, each landing on what came before. A real hand would hold
# the button: a click every quarter of a second.
aim 4 0 -1
assert crosshair != none
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 5
tap place
tick 40
assert falling == 0
assert queued == 0
assert vanished == 0
assert powder_moves > 0
state poured
surface -2 -7 12 7 -2 6
state on_the_beach
shot walk_0_the_pile_from_the_foot

# ---- walk up it, and down the far side -----------------------------------------
lookaxis +i 0
state before_walk
hold w 0.5
assert on_ground == true
assert alt_agl > 1.5
state on_the_pile
shot walk_1_on_top
hold w 0.6
assert on_ground == true
assert alt_agl < 1.5
state going_down
shot walk_2_going_down
hold w 0.6
assert on_ground == true
shot walk_3_at_the_foot
hold w 1.0
assert on_ground == true
state past_it
lookaxis -i 10
shot walk_4_looking_back

# ---- back, a jump on the way, a sprint ------------------------------------------
hold w+shift 0.6
hold w,space 0.5
assert vanished == 0
hold w 0.8
assert on_ground == true
shot walk_5_back_on_it

# ---- dig into it ----------------------------------------------------------------
aim 2 0 -1
assert crosshair == sand
state before_dig
tap break
tick 40
assert queued == 0
state after_dig
aim 2 0 -1
assert crosshair != none
tap break
tick 40
assert queued == 0
shot walk_6_dug
assert on_ground == true

# ---- save and quit, and come back -------------------------------------------------
save
reload
assert powder_moves >= 0
wait 0.5
assert on_ground == true
shot walk_7_reloaded

replay stop
assert replay_notes == 0
replay check b7-walk.replay
assert replay_ok == true
state final
